{
  "slug": "artist:jeezy",
  "name": "Jeezy",
  "editorial_article": "Jay Wayne Jenkins, known as Jeezy, rose from Hawkinsville and Atlanta to help define the trap music subgenre alongside T.I. and Gucci Mane in the mid-2000s. His 2005 Def Jam debut, Let's Get It: Thug Motivation 101, peaked at number two on the Billboard 200 and secured double platinum status, propelled by the Akon-assisted single Soul Survivor. The 2008 release The Recession topped the Billboard 200 and featured the Kanye West collaboration Put On, earning a Grammy nomination for Best Rap Performance by a duo. Throughout his career, Jeezy maintained the Corporate Thugz Entertainment (CTE World) label, signing artists such as YG and Freddie Gibbs. His discography includes later chart-topping records like 2016's Trap or Die 3. Beyond music, he famously opened his home to Hurricane Katrina victims and has ventured into film roles, including 2024's Trap City.",
